[[File:Mysterious_Old_Man.webp|right|thumb|A player interacting with the Mysterious Old Man.]]
The '''Mysterious Old Man''' teleports players to the [[Maze]] and [[Mime (Random Event)|Mime]] [[random event]]s, or simply hands out items in a similar way to [[Rick Turpentine]], because he was feeling lonely. In the Maze random event, complete the labyrinth as quickly as possible, faster for better rewards. In the Mime random event, copy the [[emotes]] of the [[Mime|mime artist]].

The Mysterious Old Man can also appear underwater, in which case he will always award an item straight away, rather than offer the player a chance to participate in an event.

Before the [[Update:Optional Randoms & Goblins|Optional Randoms update]], he would also occasionally give the player a [[strange box]] instead of teleporting them off to the Maze or the Mime, unless their inventory was full. The strange box presented the player with a puzzle asking them which shape contains which number or which number is in which shape. The rewards from this random could be very generous, as you could get a [[tooth half of key|tooth half]] or [[loop half of key|loop half]] of a [[crystal key]] from the [[Strange box|Mysterious prize box]]. The man obtained these boxes from a village in the [[Eastern Lands]].{{CitePostbag|issue=1|letter=Letter 9|author=Mysterious Old Man}}

